\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Oman's labour market operates under the updated Labour Law (Royal Decree No. 53/2023), effective 2024\hich\f31506 \endash \loch\f31506 
2025, prioritizing Omanization and strict written contract requirements. Key aspects include a 48-hour maximum work week, 6-month max probation for expat\hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 
s, 30-day notice for termination, and specialized contract types. Mandatory registration of employment contracts for non-Omanis is handled via the Ministry of Labour.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Gov.om
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 +4
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Key Aspects of the Oman Labour Agreement (2025\hich\f31506 \endash \loch\f31506 2026)
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Contract Types: Recognizes four types: Temporary (max 2 years), Permanent, Seasonal, and Part-time.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Automatic Conversion: Fixed-term contracts automatically become permanent after 5 years, or if they continue past their expiration.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Probation Period: Maximum 6 months for expatriates; 3 months for Omani workers.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Working Hours & Overtime: Maximum 8 hours/day or 48 hours/week. Overtime is paid at 1.25x (regular) or 1.5x (weekends/holidays).
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Termination: Requires 30 days\hich\f31506 \rquote \loch\f31506  written notice. Arbitrary termination compensation is capped at 12 months' pay.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Leaves: 98 days paid maternity leave; 7 days paternity leave. Sick leave is up to 182 days (paid at varying rates).
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Expat Rights: Employees can change employers if their contract is not registered with the ministry within 30 days of hiring.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 Omanization Requirement: Employers must prioritize hiring Omanis. Termination of expats can be justified by replacement with a qualified Omani national.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 End of Service Benefits: Gratuity is determined by length of service; a new "savings fund" system for expats is in place, replacing older gratuity calculations for certain sectors.
\par \hich\af31506\dbch\af31505\loch\f31506 The British Omani Society
